<title>USA: U.S. Sept natgas stocks rise 11 pct. pts to 69 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept natgas stocks rise 11 pct. pts to 69 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. natural gas storage levels in September rose 11 percentage points to 69 percent of capacity, as relatively mild weather and cheap prices encouraged operators to step up the pace of injections ahead of winter.</p>
<p>The Reuter survey of 22 firms with working gas capacity of 1.57 trillion cubic feet (tcf) showed stocks of 1.09 tcf were still about six points, or eight percent, below year-ago.</p>
<p>Last month, spot gas prices at Henry Hub, the NYMEX delivery point in Erath, La., averaged $1.80/mmBtu, 35 cents below August's average, according to Reuter data.</p>
<p>--J Silha, New York Power Desk 212-859-1624</p>
